claim.claim-text:
performing first quantizing by quantizing normalized spectral data for each non-zero band by using uniform scalar quantization, 'USQ', wherein a number of bits allocated for quantization of each band is determined in advance;
performing second quantizing by quantizing a least significant bit, "LSB', of the quantized normalized spectral data by using Trellis coded quantization, 'TCQ', wherein a number of bits used for TCQ in the second quantizing is extracted from each non-zero band evenly, and wherein USQ is then performed on the band by using the remaining number of bits in the non-zero band;
performing first arithmetic lossless coding on information about important spectral components, 'ISCs', included in the band, said information including a number, a position and a sign of the ISCs;
performing second arithmetic lossless coding on magnitude information which is constructed by the bit(s) that remain by excluding the LSB in the quantized spectral data;
performing third arithmetic lossless coding on trellis path data obtained from the second quantizing, wherein the trellis path data is encoded as equi-probable symbols, and wherein the trellis path data is a binary sequence and is encoded using an arithmetic encoder with a uniform probability model; and
generating a bitstream by using data provided from the first arithmetic lossless coding, the second arithmetic lossless coding, and the third arithmetic lossless coding,
wherein the second quantizing includes:
extracting residual data based on the difference between the quantized non-zero normalized spectral data provided from the first quantizing and original non-zero spectral data, wherein the residual data corresponds an LSB of the quantized non-zero spectral data;
constructing, for all bands that have non-zero data after quantization, a residual array by collecting the difference between the quantized non-zero spectral data and the original non-zero spectral data for all non-zero bands; and
performing TCQ on the residual array with code rate 1/2 known (7, 5)<8> code,
